/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (This study investigated the knowledge, practices, and perceptions of the academic community and the external public regarding digital security and the Brazilian General Data Protection Law \(LGPD\), relating the findings to Sustainable Development Goals \(SDGs\) 4, 9, and 16. This is an applied, descriptive study with a mixed-methods \(quantitative-qualitative\) approach, conducted through an online questionnaire with a non-probabilistic convenience sample of 25 participants, consisting of 15 affiliated with UNIG and 10 from the external public. Data were analyzed using descriptive statistics. The results show that 68% of participants use two-factor authentication on all or almost all important accounts, and 60% state they know what the LGPD is and understand their rights; however, only 28% reported feeling secure regarding the protection of their personal data. Computing was perceived positively: 96% agreed that it )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
